      "children": [
        {
          "id": "SP_KETEIODOROS_BELLENSE_STRUSZ_PERCIVAL_WRIGHT_PICKETT_BYRNES_1998",
          "name": "Keteiodoros bellense Strusz, Percival, Wright, Pickett & Byrnes, 1998",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Keteiodoros",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "mm), a low flange develops on the inner edge of each ventral valve margin which fits into a groove near the inner edge of each dorsal valve margin. The inner edges of the grooves disappearforwards, leaving the tapered outer edges of the dorsal valve margins resting against the outer surfaces of the ventral flanges. The flanges in turn become lower, the ventral valve margins narrow, and from about the shell mid-length the commissure assumes a more conventional appearance, without any overlap of dorsal valve over ventral valve. Ventral interior: The ventral platform is strongly developed, about 40 % as high as the valve and occupying about a third of the total width anteriorly. It extends well beyond mid-length, and covers a large cavity which is divided into two long vaults by an even longer median septum which may reach the start of the anteroventral sulcus. In cross-section the sides are steep to slightly overhanging, and gently convex, while the upper surface is a broad shallow trough which longitudinal sections and the excavated shell show is not a continuous smooth curve in front of the contact zone with the dorsal umbo, but terraced, the faces of the terraces facing forward.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:11164772",
          "authorship": "Strusz, Percival, Wright, Pickett & Byrnes",
          "yearPublished": "1998",
          "children": [],
